  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 135 AM EDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThursday will probably be the 'coolest' and 'wettest' of the\nperiod as the ridge axis will be furthest west and will be\nawaiting the northern stream shortwave to begin the amplification\nof the ridge pattern. It'll still be hot, with highs generally in\nthe middle 90s and heat indices nearing advisory levels, though\nthere will probably be fewer upper 90 degree readings. With at\nleast some component of northerly flow expected on Thursday, we'll\nlikely see the breezes pinned closer to the coast. However, we'll\nalso be more likely to see storms advect into the region from\ncentral Florida late in the day. Overall, coverage is expected to\nbe highest on Thursday. The end of the week and into the weekend\nwill feature the presence of the SAL once again and anomalous\nheights. Essentially another period of warmer and drier than\nnormal conditions are expected.",
